// Auto-generated from a traced tail-swish GIF (16 frames, scratchpad/tailframes) —
// each frame skeletonized (Zhang-Suen thinning), walked into an ordered centerline,
// arc-length resampled to 16 shared points, and fit through a Catmull-Rom-to-cubic-
// Bezier spline. Every frame has the exact same M + 15xC command structure (only the
// coordinates differ), which is what lets a plain keyframed animation of the `d`
// attribute morph smoothly between them instead of snapping — see TailSwish.tsx.
// Point 0 (the M) is always the tail's own anchor/base end; the far end is the tip.
//
// Doubled to 32 frames by inserting one synthetic midpoint between every pair of
// the original 16 (a straight per-point blend of their two 16-point centerlines,
// refit through the same Catmull-Rom spline) — halving the shape-change each
// keyframe step covers. At 16 frames, the segments spanning the biggest shape
// change would occasionally interpolate through a transient pinch/cusp (Motion
// blends each of the ~90 numbers in the `d` string independently and linearly;
// for two sufficiently different curve shapes, that doesn't correspond to a
// smooth physical bend), which read as the swish briefly reversing direction.
// Smaller per-step changes make that far less likely to be visible.
